# Product audience — 1 persona → 1 product

Personas live on one product’s `_product.yml` only. Canonical MCP policy: `mcp-server/explain/product.md` (Audience).

## Push back

If asked to build or design any of the following, **push back** and do not implement unless staff explicitly overturn this policy in writing:

- A shared/global persona catalog
- Multi-product membership for one persona
- Reusing the same persona id across products “because it’s the same buyer”
- Architecture that merges personas across SKUs

## Correct alternative

Same human segment on two offers (e.g. non-tech pro → Flex *or* AI Engineering) ⇒ **two product-specific personas** with different ids, fears, and objections. The 1:1 constraint forces a personalized funnel per offer.

Funnel multi-bind `{ product, persona }` rows mean different product-owned personas — not one persona attached to two products. See also `mcp-server/explain/funnel-classification-proposals.md`.
